                "service_name": "zero.rocicorp.dev"
            },
            {
                "image_url": "https://livestore.dev/opengraph-image.jpg",
                "image_width": 1200,
                "image_height": 630,
                "image_bytes": 119075,
                "from_url": "https://livestore.dev/",
                "id": 2,
                "original_url": "https://livestore.dev/",
                "fallback": "LiveStore: Local-first data layer for high-performance apps",
                "text": "LiveStore is a state management framework based on SQLite and event-sourcing. It\u2019s designed for demanding applications and based on years of research.",
                "title": "LiveStore: Local-first data layer for high-performance apps",
                "title_link": "https://livestore.dev/",
                "service_name": "livestore.dev"
            }
        ],
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "CEB1Y",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "not sure if I understand the connection to React/Vue/Svelte. They are not network technologies.\n\nI worked on the Firebase realtime database in 2014 which was a causally consistent event driven database. We now have "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "http://convex.dev",
                                "text": "convex.dev"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " or "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "https://zero.rocicorp.dev/",
                                "text": "zero"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " or "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "https://livestore.dev/",
                                "text": "livestore"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " which are successors aimed at application building.\n\nNone of them are really distributed in the fault tolerant sense. I also worked on Firestore which "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "was",
                                "style": {
                                    "italic": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " actually geographically fault tolerant (5 nines availability!) but it is so complex it requires a mega corp to cosntruct (its built on some of the same infra as Google Spanner). I feel like Firestore probably is the state of the art in true distributed reactive databases but its not necessarily the one I would choose to build an app with, but technologically it is impressive."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
